pi.github.com/users/juancho275/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/commits/f25234f0a34a3a1d1220f9e18ae0757bdf93cc12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T06:26:40Z","email":"juan.viteri@quind.io","name":"juan.viteri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T06:26:40Z","email":"juan.viteri@quind.io","name":"juan.viteri"},"message":"feat: simulate payment gateway with 10s delay — orders auto-confirm via Spring Modulith Outbox\n\nSe agrego el modulo payment que actua como simulador de pasarela de pago. Al crear una orden, el evento OrderPlaced viaja por el Outbox de Spring Modulith. El PaymentSimulatorListener lo recibe de forma asincrona, espera 10 segundos simulando el procesamiento del pago, y llama a OrderService.confirmOrder() para transicionar la orden de PENDING a CONFIRMED.\n\nEsto demuestra el patron Outbox en accion: la orden nace en PENDING, y unos segundos despues el sistema la confirma de forma autonoma sin que el usuario tenga que hacer nada. La comunicacion entre el modulo payment y el modulo order ocurre exclusivamente a traves del evento publicado, respetando los limites de modulos de Spring Modulith.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a44bec9055a18dc07170b98db2d6c0bfa97c46e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/git/trees/9a44bec9055a18dc07170b98db2d6c0bfa97c46e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/git/commits/f25234f0a34a3a1d1220f9e18ae0757bdf93cc12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90466431?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/events{/privacy}","followers_url":