pi.github.com/users/juancho275","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/commits/e21c8a6d6261148e10833f26e0c08d59e03db8bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T05:24:57Z","email":"juan.viteri@quind.io","name":"juan.viteri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T05:24:57Z","email":"juan.viteri@quind.io","name":"juan.viteri"},"message":"feat(SCRUM-30): add observability — structured logging, custom metrics and correlation IDs\n\nEvery request now gets a unique traceId attached to all its log lines (via MDC)\nand returned in the X-Trace-Id response header, making it straightforward to\ntrace a specific request through Railway logs.\n\nTwo business metrics are now tracked in Micrometer: orders.placed counts every\nsuccessful checkout, and cart.items.added counts every product added to a cart.\nBoth are tagged with the application name and available at /actuator/prometheus,\nwhich is now exposed in production alongside health and metrics.\n\nIn production, logs are emitted in ECS JSON format so they can be parsed by any\nlog aggregation tool (Elastic, Datadog, Railway structured logs).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc2c0769065dd1cfafdc5466825d82c46904011d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/git/trees/cc2c0769065dd1cfafdc5466825d82c46904011d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/git/commits/e21c8a6d6261148e10833f26e0c08d59e03db8bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90466431?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/gists{/gist_id