:"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juancho275","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/commits/ec68abc14a43bdeb0521b1e6597a8a94f71d3f2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T23:50:26Z","email":"juan.viteri@quind.io","name":"juan.viteri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T23:50:26Z","email":"juan.viteri@quind.io","name":"juan.viteri"},"message":"feat(notifications): add Notifications module as 5th Spring Modulith bounded context\n\n- New module: com.tractorstore.notifications with @ApplicationModule declaration\n- OrderNotificationListener listens to OrderPlaced event via @ApplicationModuleListener\n  (same cross-module pattern as Inventory, runs after commit in its own transaction)\n- NotificationService sends order confirmation email via JavaMailSender when SMTP\n  is configured (Railway env vars), falls back to ASCII-safe console preview otherwise\n- HTML email body with proper UTF-8 for email clients; console log uses NFD\n  normalization to strip diacritics (Windows CP850 safe)\n- Add spring-boot-starter-mail dependency to pom.xml\n- Configure smtp.auth and starttls in application.yml; SMTP credentials via\n  Railway env vars (SPRING_MAIL_HOST, SPRING_MAIL_USERNAME, SPRING_MAIL_PASSWORD)\n- 2 unit tests: NotificationServiceTest, OrderNotificationListenerTest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae6e52a65c9b411d0d1be9fdeaa8061e398823c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/git/trees/ae6e52a65c9b411d0d1be9fdeaa8061e398823c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juancho275/tractor-store/git/commits/ec68abc14a43bdeb0521b1e6597a8a94f71d3f2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_u